body:
@annefou, if you have some time it would be great if you could have a look at this (but this is definitely not too urgent, I won't be working on this before Wednesday).

From the functions you were using in the gridlook code only `bit_combine` is missing, which I think should be easy enough to expose (and potentially the rest of the API, although I have those very low on my list of priorities).

I've tried to create a namespaced API (i.e. `healpixGeo[indexingScheme].vertex`), but couldn't quite convince `wasm-bindgen` / `wasm-pack` to expose the namespaces (hence why I'm using `js_name` instead of `js_namespace`... if you have any advice here that would be helpful). This means that to have a namespaced API users have to categorize the functions in user code, which is pretty clumsy.

@pablo-richard @cgueguen 

Can we merge this?  Or with the update of documentation done recently it is already there? 

thanks
